    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (83.27) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.75), who represent our strongest offensive upside today. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from an excellent matchup against Michael McGreevy; while the official lineup is pending, his projected slot in the 3-hole combined with a strong platoon edge makes him our primary engine for Runs and SBs. **Mickey Moniak** is riding high on a massive park factor boost and a favorable platoon advantage against Brady Singer, projecting as an elite play despite being lower in the standard hierarchy. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (75.01) also deserves recognition, as his deep-seated platoon advantage against Martin Perez (King) and the current SP\u2019s xERA of 4.49 creates a high-floor profile for RBI production.\n\nStrategic optimization favored **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90) and **Austin Riley** (67.59) for their specific environmental edges. **Seiya Suzuki** is bolstered by favorable wind conditions and a park factor that elevates his base projection, while **Austin Riley** remains a high-value start due to his proximity to an exploitable 4.93 xERA, though he carries a \u26a0\ufe0f Rain Risk (30%) that owners should monitor leading up to first pitch. **James Wood** (66.63) remains a critical inclusion; despite facing a difficult catcher, his elite xwOBA and lead-off spot solidify his role in our pursuit of scarcity-driven category wins. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Josh Naylor** (58.63), who fell just shy of the threshold. While **Josh Naylor** had a decent platoon outlook, the combined efficiency of our utilized outfielders\u2014specifically the speed-centric profiles\u2014tipped the scale against him. \n\nWe are proceeding with caution regarding **Dalton Rushing** (49.00) and **Edwin Arroyo** (49.68), both of whom are borderline starts today. **Dalton Rushing** faces a difficult task against Gerrit Cole, and while **Edwin Arroyo** benefits from a park factor boost, both sit at the low end of our recommended spectrum. We have deliberately benched **Isaac Paredes** (48.94), **Zach McKinstry** (45.11), and **Henry Bolte** (43.48) to manage our game caps, as their projected outputs do not sufficiently overcome the opportunity cost relative to our primary starters. We remain fully committed to the high-speed, high-platoon efficiency model as we track the remaining lineup confirmations for **Gabriel Moreno**, **James Wood**, and **Corbin Carroll**.",
